<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Phase 3 Best in Slot Gear list for Feral Druid DPS in Wrath of the Lich King Classic. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from Trial of the Grand Crusader, Onyxia's Lair, and Ulduar. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">Best in Slot Gear for Feral Druid DPS Phase 3</h2>Just as in Phase 1 and 2, item level remains the single most impactful attribute on any piece of gear in Phase 3, as it directly determines the total allocation of useful DPS stats on each item. This means that you can continue to use item level as an excellent proxy for DPS value when evaluating potential upgrades for your Feral Druid in Phase 3. Aside from the cloak rewards for completing <a class="icontiny" data-game="wow" data-type="achievement" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/achievement=3819/a-tribute-to-insanity-25-player">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_crown_13.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">A Tribute to Insanity (25 player)</span></a>, the highest item level that is attainable from Phase 3 raid drops is 258 (from 25-man Heroic difficulty bosses in <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4722/trial-of-the-crusader">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Trial of the Crusader</span></a>), and unsurprisingly, the embedded BiS setups below use a 258 Item Level piece in nearly every slot where one is available.<br/>
<br/>Similar to Phase 2, the only scenario where deviating from maximum item level is optimal for Phase 3 gearing is when you are limited by the 8% Hit cap or 6.5% Expertise cap. Many of the new 258 Item Level drops from Heroic <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4722/trial-of-the-crusader">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Trial of the Crusader</span></a> are overloaded in Hit Rating or Expertise Rating, so you will sometimes be forced to equip a lower item level piece in order to stay below the respective caps for these stats. For example, in the embedded <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/side_alliance.gif");'></span>
<span class="q3">Alliance</span> BiS setup below, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45611/solar-bindings">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bracer_26.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Solar Bindings</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47945/gloves-of-the-silver-assassin">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlets_77a.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gloves of the Silver Assassin</span></a> are used instead of <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47155/bracers-of-dark-determination">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bracer_23b.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bracers of Dark Determination</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=48203/malfurions-handgrips-of-triumph">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlets_77b.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Malfurion's Handgrips of Triumph</span></a>, respectively, despite the higher item level on the latter two items, since the Hit Rating on these pieces cannot be efficiently utilized without exceeding 7% Hit (the reduced cap with <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=28878/heroic-presence">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_21.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Heroic Presence</span></a>). Likewise, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45536/legguards-of-cunning-deception">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_leather_28.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Legguards of Cunning Deception</span></a> are used in lieu of <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46975/leggings-of-the-broken-beast">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_leather_28.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leggings of the Broken Beast</span></a> in the <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/side_horde.gif");'></span>
<span class="q10">Horde</span> BiS setup for the same reason.<br/>
<br/>The only other change from Phase 2 gearing priorities is the introduction of a new stat cap to pay attention to: the <i>Crit soft cap</i>. If you read our <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/guide/classes/druid/feral/dps-bis-gear-pve-phase-2">Phase 2 BiS guide</a>, you should already be familiar with the concept of the Armor Penetration soft cap, which is the point at which a <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40256/grim-toll">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_trinket_naxxramas04.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Grim Toll</span></a> or <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45931/mjolnir-runestone">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_rune_11.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mjolnir Runestone</span></a> proc will boost you to the maximum useful Armor Penetration Rating value of 1399. Once you hit the soft cap (which is 648 Armor Penetration Rating with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45931/mjolnir-runestone">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_rune_11.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mjolnir Runestone</span></a>), the value of additional Armor Penetration falls below that of other stats like Strength or Agility. This same exact concept also applies to Crit, which exhibits a soft cap at 80.8% (fully raid buffed). Above this point, every single auto-attack that lands will either be a critical strike or a glancing blow, so further increases in crit chance will only benefit your special abilities. The Agility procs from <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47668/idol-of-mutilation">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_qirajidol_strife.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Idol of Mutilation</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47131/deaths-verdict">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_bone_skull_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Death's Verdict</span></a> /<wbr/> <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47464/deaths-choice">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_bone_skull_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Death's Choice</span></a> further lower the Crit soft cap to 70.67%, which becomes achievable when fully raid buffed in Phase 3 gear.<br/>
<br/>Just like Phase 2, the main practical consequence of the Armor Penetration and Crit soft caps comes in the form of gem selection for your gear, rather than in the items themselves. The general rules of thumb for Phase 3 gemming are as follows:<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Use <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40117/fractured-cardinal-ruby">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_37.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fractured Cardinal Ruby</span></a> gems in all red sockets until you hit the Armor Penetration soft cap.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Next, use <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40118/precise-cardinal-ruby">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_37.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Precise Cardinal Ruby</span></a>, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40125/rigid-kings-amber">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_38.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rigid King's Amber</span></a>, and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40162/accurate-ametrine">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_39.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Accurate Ametrine</span></a> gems until you are just below the Hit and Expertise caps.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Then, use <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40112/delicate-cardinal-ruby">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_37.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Delicate Cardinal Ruby</span></a> in red sockets and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40142/inscribed-ametrine">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_39.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Inscribed Ametrine</span></a> in yellow sockets until you reach the relevant Crit soft cap for your gear setup.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Finally, fill all remaining red sockets with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40111/bold-cardinal-ruby">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_37.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bold Cardinal Ruby</span></a> and all remaining yellow sockets with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40146/fierce-ametrine">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_39.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fierce Ametrine</span></a>, as these become the highest value gems above the Crit soft cap.</div></li></ol>With these gearing priorities in mind, shown below are the absolute highest DPS gear configurations that can be assembled by a Feral Druid in Phase 3.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="alliance">Alliance BiS</h3>
