<br/>
<br/>Note that the above BiS setups include the Engineering-exclusive enchants <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=55016/nitro-boosts">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nitro Boosts</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=54999/hyperspeed-accelerators">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Hyperspeed Accelerators</span></a>, and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=55002/flexweave-underlay">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Flexweave Underlay</span></a>. As mentioned in our <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/guide/classes/druid/feral/dps-overview-pve#best-professions">class overview guide</a>, <a class="icontiny" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/skill=202/engineering">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Engineering</span></a> is such an insanely overpowered profession for PvE that it is assumed that any competitive Feral DPS player will have it. In contrast, your second profession choice has hardly any impact in WotLK since all crafting professions provide very comparable PvE benefits, so no other profession-exclusive gear augmentations are assumed.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="emblems">Emblems of Triumph for Feral Druid DPS Phase 3</h3>The only <a class="icontiny q1" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=301/emblem-of-triumph">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_summonchampion.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Triumph</span></span></a> reward in the BiS gear setups shown above is <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47668/idol-of-mutilation">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_qirajidol_strife.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Idol of Mutilation</span></a>, which provides a hefty 110 DPS increase over <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40713/idol-of-the-ravenous-beast">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_relics_idolofferocity.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Idol of the Ravenous Beast</span></a> and should be a priority to obtain early on in the phase. The other rewards are all outclassed by 258 Item Level drops from 25-man Heroic bosses, but can serve as solid intermediate upgrades while you are waiting for the BiS option to drop. In particular, once you have purchased <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47668/idol-of-mutilation">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_qirajidol_strife.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Idol of Mutilation</span></a>, it is recommended to save up 120 Emblems so that you can purchase the 245 Item Level version of the Tier 9 helm and shoulders as soon as possible after obtaining 2x <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47242/trophy-of-the-crusade">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_trophy_argent.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Trophy of the Crusade</span></a> from raids. Note that it is <i>not</i> recommended to spend any of your Emblems on the 232 Item Level ("of Conquest") versions of the Tier 9 pieces, as these are simply too minor of an upgrade from Tier 8 and will delay you from obtaining the more impactful 245 pieces.<br/>
<br/>
