<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="weapons">Weapons and Idols for Feral Druid DPS Phase 3</h2>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="weapons-for-feral-druid-dps-phase-3">Weapons for Feral Druid DPS Phase 3</h4>The weapon slot mirrors the glove and leg slots in having two nearly identical value options to choose from in Phase 3: a staff off the Twin Val'kyr, and a polearm off Anub'arak, both on 25-man Heroic difficulty. Neither weapon has Hit Rating on it, so they should be viewed as truly interchangeable options for both factions, and in practice you should stick with whichever one you can obtain first. <br/>
<br/>However, the weapon you end up using does have consequences on optimal gemming for the rest of your gear set due to the Crit soft cap: setups built around the polearm will tend to use more Strength and Haste gems to accommodate the 102 Critical Strike Rating on it, while setups built around the staff can fit more Agility and Crit gems. You will notice that the full BiS embedded setups at the top of this guide use <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47239/archon-glaive">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_staff_101.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Archon Glaive</span></a> for <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/side_alliance.gif");'></span>
<span class="q3">Alliance</span> (with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40146/fierce-ametrine">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_39.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fierce Ametrine</span></a> in most yellow sockets)  and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47463/twins-pact">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_staff_97.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Twin's Pact</span></a> for <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/side_horde.gif");'></span>
<span class="q10">Horde</span> (with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40142/inscribed-ametrine">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_39.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Inscribed Ametrine</span></a> in all yellow sockets). This is an <i>extremely minor</i> faction-specific optimization, and enables both setups to hover tightly around the Crit soft cap without overly exceeding it.<br/>
<br/>
<b>Recommended BiS Weapon Enchant</b>: <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=59621/enchant-weapon-berserking">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_enchant_formulasuperior_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Weapon - Berserking</span></a>
<br/>Note that <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=60691/enchant-2h-weapon-massacre">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_enchant_formulasuperior_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant 2H Weapon - Massacre</span></a> is only very slightly worse for average DPS value, so it is the preferred enchant for weapons that you will also be using while tanking.<div class="pad"></div>
